What the M5 Brings to This Pipeline

The M5 is a significant leap specifically for this kind of workload. The key findings are:

GPU: The M5's 10-core GPU has a Neural Accelerator embedded in every single GPU core — this is new architecture, not just a speed bump. It delivers 4x peak GPU compute over M4 and is explicitly designed for mixed ML + graphics workloads like exactly what this pipeline does.

Memory Bandwidth: Apple's own MLX research benchmarks show 19–27% performance improvement over M4 specifically for ML inference workloads running on MLX. Since the entire depth estimation and image processing stack uses MLX and Metal, you benefit from all of it.

Neural Engine: The M5 carries a 16-core Neural Engine, which handles depth model inference independently, freeing GPU cores for the layer compositing and motion work happening simultaneously.

Unified Memory: The critical advantage for this pipeline is that all 16GB is shared between CPU, GPU, and Neural Engine with no data transfer bottleneck. On a discrete GPU setup you'd lose 1-2 seconds just moving tensors — on M5 that cost is near zero.

